senses.gloss:
शार॑ f. आ mottled, spotted;
 m. a stone or piece used at
sev. games (also f. ई).

सर॑ a. fluid, liquid;
 (f. ई) running, moving, going
(—˚). f. सरा॑ brook, सरी waterfall.

2 सा॑र m. n. the interior firm parts of a body;
 firmness,
solidity, strength;
 property, wealth;
 substance or essence of anything;
nectar;
 water.

शरच्चन्द्र m. the autumnal moon;
 ˚च्चन्द्रिका f. the
autumnal moon-shine.

2 शरण॑ a. protecting, guarding;
 n. protection, refuge or
place of refuge, shelter, shed, hut, dwelling, abode;
 ˚णं गम् have
recourse to (gen. or acc.).

शरण्य a. affording or seeking protection, refuge, or
help;
 abstr. ˚ता f.

शरभ॑ m. a kind of deer, later a fabulous eight-legged
animal;
 E. of Viṣṇu, N. of an Asura etc.

शरव्य n. aim, abstr. ˚ता f.;
 ˚व्या॑ f. arrow-shot or
hail of arrows.

शराव m. n. a flat earthenware dish;
 also a measure for
grain.

शरावर m. a quiver;
 n. shield or coat of mail (also
˚वरण n.).

शरावसंपात m. the appearance of dishes (at a
meal);
 ˚ते वृत्ते when this is past, i.e. after meals.

स॑रस a. juicy, moist, humid, fresh, new, tasty,
pleasant, charming, passionate, enamoured;
 n. adv. with rapture.

श॑रीर n. (m.) the body, also = person;
 abstr. ˚ता† f.,
˚त्व† n.

शारीर॑ f. ई made of bone;
 corporeal, of the body. n.
bodily constitution, excrement.

शरीरवन्त् a. having a body, bodily, solid, firm;
 m. a
living creature.

शरीरिन् a. having a body or having (—˚) for body;
 m.
living creature, man, soul.

श॑र्कर a. consisting of gravel or grit;
 m. pebble, also
= f. श॑र्करा gravel, grit, brown sugar.

शर्ध् श॑र्धति fart (only w. अव & वि);
 be defiant or
strong.

सार्ध a. with a half;
 n. सार्ध॑म् adv. together, along
with (instr. or —˚).

श॑र्य m. arrow, dart;
 f. आ reed, arrow, p matting of reed
(on the Soma-strainer).

*शर्यण a. thicket of reeds;
 m. pl. N. of a region in
Kurukṣetra.

शार्व f. ई relating to Śarva (Śiva);
 w. दिश् f. the
north-east.

स॑र्व a. whole, entire, all;
 m. sgl. everyone, pl. all (w.
अपि all together);
 n. sgl. everything. — With a neg. not every, not
every one or everything, no, nothing.

शर्वपर्वत m. Śarva's mountain, i.e. Kailāsa.
(*शर्वर a. spotted);
 f. श॑र्वरी pl. the spotted deer (of the
Maruts);
 sgl. the (starred) night.

सार॑ङ्ग dappled;
 relating to the dappled antelope. m. a
kind of antelope, sev. birds, a bee.

सारङ्ग॑, f. dappled;
 relating to the dappled antelope.
m. a kind of antelope, sev. birds, a bee.

स॑र्ग m. shot (lit. & fig.), jet or gush (of water etc.);
letting loose, pouring out;
 a herd let loose from the stall, i.g. swarm,
host, multitude;
 creation, creature, begetting, offspring, child;
origin, nature, character;
 purpose, resolution;
 chapter of an epic poem.

शार्ङ्ग a. made of horn or coming from the Cṛṅga-tree. m.
a cert. bird (f. ई);
 n. bow (esp. that of Viṣṇu).

शार्ङ्गधर m. the same;
 N. of an author, ˚पद्धति
f. his work.

सरण्यु॑ a. speedy, quick;
 f. ऊ॑ N. of a daughter of
Tvaṣṭṛ.

सरल a. straight, direct, candid, honest;
 m. & f. आ
names of trees.

सराग a. coloured, reddened;
 pleasant, charming;
passionate, enamoured;
 n. adv.

सरुज् a. suffering (the same) pain or sickness;
 ill,
diseased.

सरुज a. causing or suffering pain, unwell;
 abstr. ˚त्व
n.

स॑रूप a. of the same shape or form with (gen. or —˚);
like, similar;
 shaped, formed, embodied;
 beautiful, handsome.

†सर्ज m. turner, twister (cf. रज्जुसर्ज॑);
 N. of a tree
& its resin.

सर्वंसह a. bearing or enduring all;
 f. आ the
earth.

सर्वज्ञ a. all-knowing, all-wise;
 abstr. ˚ता f.,
˚त्व n.

सर्व॑तस् adv. from or on all sides;
 everywhere, wholly,
entirely;
 as prep. *around (acc.).

सर्व॑ताति f. wholeness, completeness, integrity;
 loc.
˚ताता on the whole, at all.

सर्व॑तोमुख f. ई (having the face) turned
everywhere;
 all-sided, complete, perfect.

सर्व॑त्र adv. everywhere, always, by all means;
 w. neg.
in no case, by no means.

सर्वप्रायश्चित्त॑ f. ई॑ expiating or redressing
all;
 n. general expiation or atonement.

सर्वभाव m. the whole heart or soul;
 ˚— & instr.
with all the heart.

सर्वभूत॑ a. being everywhere, ubiquitous;
 n. pl. all
beings.

सर्वमङ्गल a. all-auspicious;
 f. आ E. of Durgā
and Lakṣmī.

1 सर्वरस m. fluids or juices of every kind (pl. or
—˚);
 every taste or flavour;
 pl. dainty things of all kind.

सर्वलोक॑ m. the universe;
 all people, every one (also
pl. & —˚).

सर्वशक्ति f. the whole strength;
 instr. with all
strength.

सर्वश॑स् adv. wholly, entirely, altogether;
 by all
means, anyhow;
 always, everywhere.

सर्वशून्य a. completely empty;
 abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व
n. complete emptiness, nihilism (ph.).

सर्वस्व n. the whole property;
 the whole substance of
anything, entireness, totality.

सर्वहृद् n. the whole heart;
 instr. ˚हृदा with all the
heart.

1 सर्वाङ्ग n. (adj. —˚ f. ई) the whole body;
 pl. all
limbs or members.

2 स॑र्वाङ्ग f. ई having all limbs or members;
 perfect,
complete;
 n. adv.

1 सर्वात्मन् m. the whole person or essence;
 the universal
spirit (ph.), instr. with all the heart, thoroughly, perfectly.

सारघ॑ a. coming from a bee;
 m. bee;
 n. honey.

सारङ्गी dappled;
 relating to the dappled antelope. m. a
kind of antelope, sev. birds, a bee.

सारता f. ˚त्व n. firmness, solidity;
 value, worth;
highest degree.

सारफल्गु a. strong or weak, good or bad;
 abstr. ˚ता
f., ˚त्व n.

सार्थ a. having a commission or business, having a meaning
or signification;
 successful, important, rich. —m. company of traders,
caravan;
 troop, band, host, multitude i.g.

सार्थक a. useful, advantageous;
 having a sense or
meaning, abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व n.

सार्थिक a. travelling (with a caravan), accompanying
(gen.);
 merchant, trader.
